# Open-source upstreams (cloned — do NOT reimplement/decompile these)

Per the reuse strategy (docs 08–09): for anything that already exists upstream, clone it
and wire it in instead of reverse-engineering the shipped binary. These are shallow clones
(`--depth 1`) for reference + direct reuse.

| Clone | Upstream | Replaces (shipped closed binary) | License |
|---|---|---|---|
| `VINS-Mono/` | HKUST-Aerial-Robotics/VINS-Mono | `as_camera_models/libcamera_models.so` (it is **camodocal**, see `camera_model/include/camodocal/...`) | GPL-3.0 for VINS, camera_models is BSD |
| `rknn_model_zoo/` | airockchip/rknn_model_zoo | `det_ros` (YOLOv8), `seg_ros` (PP-LiteSeg) NPU deployment | Apache-2.0 / per-example |
| `open_mower_ros/` | ClemensElflein/open_mower_ros | architectural reference for `mower_logic`/`mower_map`/`mower_msgs`/`slic3r_coverage_planner` | GPL-3.0 |
| `teb_local_planner/` | rst-tu-dortmund/teb_local_planner | `teb_controller` | BSD |
| `polygon_coverage_planning/` | ethz-asl/polygon_coverage_planning | `polygon_coverage_*` | BSD |
| `spatio_temporal_voxel_layer/` | SteveMacenski/spatio_temporal_voxel_layer | `spatio_temporal_voxel_layer` | LGPL-2.1 |

## Still to clone (bigger / model-bearing — on demand)

* `PaddleSeg` (PaddlePaddle) — `seg_ros` model definition (the `.rknn` weights already ship
  in `ros2_port_handoff/11_perception_models/`).
* `ultralytics` (YOLOv8) — `det_ros` model authoring. AGPL-3.0 — review before distributing.
* WITMOTION `JY61P` sample/protocol — `libbase_imu.so` is the vendor wrapper `aichw_witimu`
  over the documented WIT JY61P serial protocol; only the thin wrapper is proprietary.

## Licensing

`open_mower_ros` (GPL-3.0) and `Ultralytics` (AGPL-3.0) are copyleft. Treat them as
reference/architecture only unless you accept those terms for the derived parts. The BSD
items (`camera_models`, `teb`, `polygon_coverage`) are safe to link directly.
