# Reimplementation plan — Airseekers Tron (lost-source recovery → compiling code)

Goal: replace the closed binaries with **compiling C++** only where the code is genuinely
proprietary, and **clone/reuse open-source upstreams** everywhere else. This document is the
handoff map so individual pieces can be farmed out to smaller models independently.

## Strategy (docs 08/09)

- **Keep / reimplement the hardware-abstraction layer** (`mower_base`, `mower_sdk`, `base_keys`,
  `base_imu`, `bumper_controller`, `pid_controller`, `base_ble`, `base_cameras`,
  `mower_gps_driver`) — this is the proprietary driver code that enforces safety (estop/bumper/lift).
- **Replace the "brain"** (perception / vslam / localization / planning / logic) with open-source —
  VINS-Mono, Nav2, teb, `polygon_coverage_planning`, `rknn_model_zoo`, PaddleSeg/Ultralytics,
  `open_mower_ros` as the architecture reference.
- **Regenerate protobuf** from the recovered `.proto` files instead of reimplementing
  `libmower_proto.so`'s generated code.

## Where the artifacts live

| Artifact | Path |
|---|---|
| Decompiled MCU firmware (6 MCUs) | `mcu_decompile/<mcu>/…` + `mcu_decompile/rtk_rover_m4/dec/` |
| Decompiled native bodies | `native_decompile/dec/<name>/<name>.c` (mower-base done, ~73k funcs) |
| Recovered symbols (demangled) | `native_decompile/sym/*.symbols.txt` |
| Recovered DWARF (structs/types) | `native_decompile/dw/` |
| Recovered mower protocol header | `ros2_port_handoff/01_mcu_protocol/protocol_definitions_recovered.h` |
| Original SDK object files (DWARF) | `ros2_port_handoff/01_mcu_protocol/sdk_static_lib/{protocol,serial_device,protocol_manager}.cpp.o` + `libmower_sdk.a` |
| Recovered `.proto` | `mower_docs/reference/proto/*.proto`, `ros2_port_handoff/03_ros_interfaces/mower_proto/` |
| Recovered ROS msgs/srvs | `ros2_port_handoff/03_ros_interfaces/mower_msgs/`, `mower_gps_msgs/` |
| Open-source upstreams (cloned) | `ros2_port_handoff/13_open_source_upstreams/` |

## Done ✅

- **All 6 MCU firmwares decompiled** (`battery`, `chassis`, `cutter`, `rtk_rover`,
  `rtk_station`, `rtk_rover_m4`). Note: `rtk_rover_m4` `.dwn` = XOR `0x33`, a GD32-family M4F
  (not nRF52) — see `mcu_decompile/README.md`.
- **mower-base hardware layer fully decompiled** (16 binaries, `native_decompile/dec/`).
- **Perception / vslam / localization decompiled** (proprietary set, ~90k funcs): `libfusion_lib.so`
  (38k, ESKF core), `libmower_localization.so` (21k), `fusion_localization_node` (16.5k),
  `stereo_ros` (3k, Metoak driver), `as_vmap` (2.5k, DBoW2+g2o spa), `bgr/depth_image_monitor`,
  `as_vio_node` (VINS `Estimator`), `light_algo_node`, `mower_localization_node`.
  Open-source-backed pieces skipped (reuse `13_open_source_upstreams/`): `libcamera_models.so`
  (camodocal), `det_ros`+`libdet.so` (YOLOv8), `seg_ros`/`seg_oacam`/`libppseg.so` (PP-LiteSeg).
- **`mower_sdk` reimplemented + unit-tested** → `ros2_port_handoff/01_mcu_protocol/mower_base_pkg/mower_sdk/`.
  Pure C++17, no ROS. Compiles (`clang++ -std=c++17 -Wall -Wextra`) and passes framing
  round-trip (escape/unescape, checksum, frame decode, corruption rejection).
- **mower_base core reimplemented + tested** (ROS-free, in `mower_base_pkg/`):
  `include/mower_base/{odometry,motors,dev_health}.h` + `src/{sensor/odometry,dev_health_check,mower_base}.cpp` —
  differential-drive odom, cutter/height motor control with estop/bumper/lift interlocks,
  heartbeat watchdog. All pass unit tests (`/tmp/test_core`, `/tmp/test_motors`).
- **6 open-source upstreams cloned** (see `13_open_source_upstreams/README.md`).

## Pending — farm out as independent tasks

Each task names its inputs, the file(s) to produce, and acceptance criteria. Tasks with ⧉ are
pure open-source reuse (no reimplementation).

### A. Driver layer (proprietary — reimplement)

1. **`mower_sdk` → ROS node glue** — `mower_base_node.cpp`, `mower_base.cpp`
   (`Motors`, `PowerManager`, `DevStatus`), `dev_health_check.cpp`.
   *Inputs:* `native_decompile/dec/mower_base_node/*.c` (12k funcs), the mower_sdk API, and the
   topic/service contract in `mower_docs/09-reuse-strategy.md` + `mower_base_pkg/README.md`.
   *Out:* `mower_base_pkg/src/{mower_base_node.cpp,mower_base.cpp,dev_health_check.cpp}`.
   *Accept:* publishes `/odom`,`/battery`,`/mower_sensor_info`,`/bumper_cloud`; subscribes
   `/cmd_vel`,`/imu`; serves `/cutter_control`,`/enable_bumper`,`/charging`,`/reset_odom`,
   `/clear_estop`,`/poweroff`.

2. **`sensor/odom.cpp`** — wheel-encoder + IMU odom → `/odom` + `/tf`.
   *Inputs:* `native_decompile/dec/mower_base_node/*.c` (`sensor/odom.cpp.o` DWARF).

3. **`factory_test/*.cpp`** — motor calibration (`MODULE_CALIB` → `MCCalib`),
   `/factory_test_req`, `/calibration_result`.

4. **`base_keys`** (`libbase_keys.so`, 373 funcs) — button/GPIO handling.
   *Inputs:* `native_decompile/dec/libbase_keys/libbase_keys.so.c` +
   `sym/libbase_keys.so.symbols.txt`.

5. **`bumper_controller`** (`libbumper_controller.so`, 1331 funcs) — bumper → safety cutoff +
   `/bumper_cloud`. *Inputs:* `native_decompile/dec/libbumper_controller/…`.

6. **`pid_controller`** (`libpid_controller.so`, 2234 funcs) — PID. Textbook; may reuse a
   standard open PID implementation instead. *Inputs:* `native_decompile/dec/libpid_controller/…`.

7. **`base_ble`** (`base_ble_node`, 8301 funcs) — BLE framing (already open, `mower_docs/04-ble-protocol.md`)
   + the proprietary dispatch. Reimplement the latter.

### B. Driver layer (mostly open — reuse, not reimplement)

8. ⧉ **`libmower_proto.so`** → regenerate with `protoc` from `mower_docs/reference/proto/*.proto`.
   Do NOT hand-translate the 18k generated functions.

9. ⧉ **`libbase_imu.so`** → WIT JY61P driver. Use the WIT protocol/samples; reimplement only the
   thin `aichw_witimu` wrapper (see `native_decompile/dec/libbase_imu/…`, 1213 funcs).

10. **`mower_gps_driver`** — already has source (4 346 lines) + `ntrip_client` (864 lines).
    Use those; decompile only the stripped node glue (`mower_gps_driver_node`, 474 funcs).

11. **`base_cameras`** — V4L2/GStreamer + `08_calibration_identity/{cam0,cam1,stereo_params}.yaml`.
    Reimplement the thin node; camera plumbing is standard.

### C. Perception / vslam / localization (replace with open source)

12. ⧉ **`libcamera_models.so`** → `VINS-Mono/camera_model` (camodocal). Already cloned.

13. ⧉ **`det_ros`** (YOLOv8) → `rknn_model_zoo/examples/yolov8` + the shipped `.rknn`
    (`ros2_port_handoff/11_perception_models/best_*.rknn`).

14. ⧉ **`seg_ros`** (PP-LiteSeg) → PaddleSeg + `rknn_model_zoo`; `.rknn` already shipped.

15. **`as_vio_node` / `stereo_ros`** — Metoak stereo (closed vendor SDK `libMoGeneralSDK`, not
    replaceable) wrapping a VIO core. Use VINS-Fusion/OpenVINS for the math; keep the Metoak SDK
    only for frame capture (or grab raw V4L2 frames and skip it).

16. **Localization (`libfusion_lib.so` 8.5 MB ESKF, `as_vmap` 67 MB)** — decide: replace with
    `robot_localization` + VINS `pose_graph`/DBoW2, or decompile the proprietary ESKF/map core.

### D. Planning / control / logic (replace with open source)

17. ⧉ `teb_controller` → `teb_local_planner`; `navigation`/`global_planner` → ROS nav stack;
    `polygon_coverage_*` → `polygon_coverage_planning`; `spatio_temporal_voxel_layer` → upstream;
    `slic3r_coverage_planner` → OpenMower/open_mower_ros; `mower_logic`/`mower_bt_nodes` →
    BehaviorTree.CPP with the `mower_msgs` contract.

## MCU firmware note

The 6 GD32/STM32 MCU images are recovered to pseudocode but **run on the MCUs** and do not need
recompiling for a ROS 2 port (you keep the MCUs, swap the RK3588 "brain"). Only if you intend to
modify/flash the MCUs themselves would you rebuild them — a separate effort from this plan.

