# 05 — Maps and the local HTTP API

## Where maps live

```
/userdata/RobotData/
├── active_map.json          id of the map in use (e.g. 24705761407971328)
├── robot.db                 SQLite: tb_map, tb_task, tb_run_task_info, tb_task_break_point_info, tb_config
├── map/
│   ├── <map_id>/
│   │   ├── map.geojson      boundaries, zones, dock points (local frame, see below)
│   │   ├── rtk_info.txt
│   │   ├── vmap/            VSLAM map (meta_map.txt + timestamped dir)
│   │   ├── spatial/         submaps
│   │   ├── layers/*.png     costmap layers: cutting, forbid, static, real_obstacle, dynamic_obstacle,
│   │   │                    inflate, outside, special_zone, blind_zone, along_border_cutting, stuck, ...
│   │   ├── cell_heatmap.png
│   │   └── spatial_distribution.png
│   └── spatial/submaps_temp
├── reports/  track.txt  bag/  voice/  upgrade/
```

There's also `/userdata/vslam/`.

### Database tables

```sql
tb_map  (id PK, name UNIQUE, geoJsonFile, userId, createdAt)
tb_task (id PK, name UNIQUE, mapId FK -> tb_map.id ON DELETE CASCADE, type, units, createdAt)
tb_config (id PK, content, createdAt)   -- e.g. DeviceLock=0, Net4GAllowUploadPicture=1
```

**Deleting a map row also deletes its tasks,** because of the cascade.

### `map.geojson` format

- Standard GeoJSON `FeatureCollection` with top-level `properties` and `version`.
- **Coordinates are in the local frame,** in metres, with the origin at the dock. The origin is the mower's rear-axle centre when its contacts sit on the charger; axes are X forward, Y left, Z up.
- **Each coordinate has 6 values,** for example `[x, y, z, roll?, pitch?, quality]`. The last is 1 for an RTK fixed solution and 2 otherwise, like `TrackPoint.quality` in `common.proto`.
- **GPS conversion** uses the charging-station GPS pose and heading from `/localization/GetMapInfo`.

`properties.type` on each feature:

| type | Geometry | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Polygon | Work area (named, e.g. "A") |
| 3 | LineString | Channel (passage between areas, or the dock→area path) |
| 4 | Polygon | Obstacle or no-go zone |
| 5 | Polygon | Dock zone or dock outline |
| 6 | Point | Charge point (`name: charge_point`) |
| 7 | Point | Undock point (`name: undock_point`) |
| 8 | Point | RTK base station |

Each feature also has `id` (a UUID), `name` and `parent_id`. The older `E_TYPE_*` names are documented in `reference/mower_map_geojson_README.md`. Sample maps are in `/workspace/src/mower_task/mower_map/maps/` and `mower_logic/task_maps/`.

## Local HTTP API — `mower_logic`, port 13344

- Listens on **`0.0.0.0:13344`, with no authentication**.
- Full spec: `reference/openapi.json`.
- `GET /map/list` was tested live and works. The other endpoints are documented from the spec but **untested**.
