# Native (aarch64) binary recovery — Airseekers Tron

The `devel/<pkg>/lib/...` ROS nodes and `.so` libraries (the closed-source compiled
layer on the RK3588) were recovered here. The binaries themselves are **complete** —
it's the source that was stripped. What's recoverable depends on how each was built:

| Build state | What survives | What I recovered |
|---|---|---|
| **DWARF debug info** (9 binaries) | source paths, every function/type/variable name, struct member offsets | near-original symbols + struct layouts → proto headers |
| **stripped `.so`** (rest) | exported dynamic symbols (`.dynsym`, mangled C++) | full public API, demangled |
| **stripped executable** | `.dynsym` + imported symbols | node graph + which `.so` APIs it calls |

> Nothing here recovers the original `.cpp` verbatim — that's impossible from compiled
> output. But the **symbol names, class/method structure, struct field names, call graph
> and control flow** *are* recovered, which is the great majority of "the lost source".

## Tooling

* `scripts/dwarfdump.py` — DWARF → sources / functions / types (needs `pyelftools`)
* `scripts/dwstruct.py` — DWARF → struct/enum member layouts (regenerates headers)
* `scripts/dynsym.py` — ELF → demangled exported/local function symbols
* Ghidra 10.4 (headless) — decompiler for logic that symbols don't cover

## The nine DWARF binaries → `dw/`

These still carry full debug info. Recovered **original source paths** (all under
`/workspace/src/...`) and complete symbol tables:

| Binary | Sources (vendor) | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `mower_sdk_test`, `mower_sdk_ncurses` | `mower_drivers/mower_base/mower_sdk/{protocol,protocol_manager,serial_device}.cpp` | **statically link the full `mower_sdk`** — richest target |
| `stereo_ros` | `mower_perception/vslam_ros/src/stereo_ros.cpp` | Metoak stereo driver node |
| `det_ros` | `mower_perception/det_ros/src/det_ros.cpp` | YOLOv8 detector node |
| `seg_ros`, `seg_oacam` | `mower_perception/seg_ros/src/{seg_ros,seg_oacam,seg_utils}.cpp` | PP-LiteSeg |
| `bgr_image_monitor`, `depth_image_monitor` | `mower_perception/image_quality/...` | image QA monitors |
| `as_vmap` (67 MB) | `mower_localization/vision_localization/vmap/src/*` | visual map; **ThirdParty/DBoW** (ORB-SLAM DBoW2), submap/pose-graph (`spa_align`) |

## Reconstructed hardware SDK (from `mower_sdk_test` DWARF) → `dw/mower_sdk_structs.structs.txt`

`namespace mower_sdk::protocol` — the exact wire structs (field names are original):

```
Heartbeat{year,month,day,hour,minute,second,ms_h,ms_l}
Version{major,minor,patch}   VersionInfo{cutter_board,chassis_board,rtk_board}
ChargeControl{enable}
MotorControl{enable,direction,speed(u16),position(u16)}
CutterControl{cutter_motor:MotorControl, height_motor:MotorControl}
SensorInfoControl{bumper,rain,lift,stop,power_off,battery_gate,cutter_size,press_module}
SensorInfo{...8 flags, bumper_r, bumper_l}
SpeedData{linear:f32, angular:f32}
MotorInfo{speed,current,voltage, temperature, status}   MotorsInfo{cutter,left,right,height}
ImuData{pitch,roll,yaw,accx..gyroz (i16×9)}   BatteryInfo{...}   Log{message}
```

`mower_sdk::Protocol` carries the frame constants `SOF/_EOF/ESCAPE/ESCAPE_SOF/ESCAPE_EOF`.
Public SDK classes/methods (recovered from demangled symbols): `SerialDevice`
(`OpenDevice/CloseDevice/ConfigDevice/Read/Write`), `ProtocolManager`
(`Start/Stop/Init/SendPacket/ReceivePacket/HandlePacket/ReceiveLoop/WriteLoop`),
`HardwareInterface`, plus `SendHeartbeat/SendSpeedData/SendImuData/SendCutterControl/
SendChargeControl/SendSensorInfoControl` and the `Set*Callback` family — this maps 1:1
